WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:02.100
Until TRIGGER's concert...

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.440
We're not performing for a month?

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.230
Kujo Tenn?

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.900
TRIGGER's center. My twin brother.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.030
Tenn-nii...

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.360
We can sing and dance now, right?

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.530
Yes.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:17.240
Some guys are promoting themselves 
to fans leaving the concert!

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.990
They're IDOLiSH7!

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:28.170
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.710
Someday we'll make it past there

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:37.850
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.140
We don't know what's right

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.350
So we Try and Jump!

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.520
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.150
For us It's Only Way!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:57.320
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.170
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.330
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.500
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.330
Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.130
In the light!

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.540
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:16.010
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.800
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.310
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:28.810
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:35.780
The future surely lies on the other side

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.700
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.080
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:48.330
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.010
Secret

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.680
A new song?

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.680
<b>Title Undecided</b>

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.760
I have another new song.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.600
It's not just yours!

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.400
Oh! <i>We</i> have another new song.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.400
It's perfect for you boys right now.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.490
I've been waiting for you to 
be ready to sing this song.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:25.360
The most important aspect of singing 
isn't technique, it's heart.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.330
And now, you can sing it.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.710
You're going to be busy learning 
the choreography, among other things.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.830
We've already scheduled the announcement.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.550
Are you ready?

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.050
Yes!

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.010
I'm off.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:52.940
Yamato-san.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:53.930
Hey.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.030
Huh? What are you doing here?

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.300
You're going to TRIGGER's 
office to apologize, right?

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.490
I'll go with you.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.670
So you knew.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.450
This is my job, though.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.040
I can't let you take all the blame.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.230
Besides, I am the leader of the group.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.580
B-But...

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:17.720
Just let me stand next to 
you like a splash guard.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:22.150
It's not something they're good at, but I am.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:27.100
When any mud gets splashed on 
IDOLiSH7, I'll stand at the front.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.730
Yamato-san, you're such a strange person.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.900
You seem like someone who does things 
his way, but you actually care about—

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.890
Wait.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.070
If you're planning on saying 
something embarrassing,

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.810
I'm turning around and 
heading back to the dorm.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:41.900
Sorry!

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:46.410
Now, shall we go get yelled at together?

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.410
Wow, Yaotome Productions 
certainly is impressive.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.900
Don't look around so much.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.920
I feel like I'm your guardian, jeez.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.140
Feeling better?

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.020
I have 21 King Puddings for you 
to take with you when you leave.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.810
Huh? Pudding?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.110
Why did you come today?

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.910
It's about the incident after the concert.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.860
Sorry. We weren't trying to steal your fans.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.270
I take pride in what happened.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:32.030
It means our concert was powerful 
enough to make you dance,

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:35.320
even if our president and 
Gaku don't see it that way.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.210
Who is she?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.250
Our manager.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.180
N-Nice to meet you.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.590
I'm Takanashi Tsumugi from
Takanashi Productions.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:50.350
I'm terribly sorry for the trouble we caused.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.490
You're Riku-san's brother, aren't you?

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.640
I'll send you tickets when IDOLiSH7 debuts.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.440
I hope you'll come see Riku-san—

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.570
That day will never come.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:04.570
Huh?

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.170
Riku has a fatal flaw.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:11.080
He can't survive in the show business world.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.840
A fatal flaw?

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.080
What does that mean?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:20.590
Tell Riku not to step into this 
world with such naive resolve.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.000
What?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.890
He's just bothering people like us
 who are taking this seriously.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.610
Good. Our timing's coming together.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.550
I wanna perform soon.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.920
Riku-kun, are you okay?

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:49.570
Huh?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.750
You seem to get tired quickly.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.730
Can you really perform a two or 
three hour concert like that?

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.210
I-I can. I can do it.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.000
I'm fine.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.320
Let's take it from the top.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.380
Excuse me.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.670
What's gotten into you?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.030
What?

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:10.840
Nanase-san, do you...

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.850
Lunch, guys.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.830
Oh, gorgeous!

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.810
It's a double fried chicken lunch.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.490
It's so luxurious.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.350
Once in a while.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.470
We'll keep working hard so we can 
have even nicer lunches soon.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.390
Hey, Ban-chan.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:34.200
You even have a nickname for Banri-san?

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.700
When will we get to be on TV?

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.190
Not for a while.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.540
Tamaki, why are you so 
interested in being on TV?

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:44.290
Because then people will see my face.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.120
How cute.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:51.250
You want to brag to your 
classmates about being on TV.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:56.560
So-chan, you're lucky you don't 
have anything to worry about.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.850
Listen up, everyone.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.590
I have something important to discuss.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.700
What? What is it?

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:04.860
Something important?

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.970
Yes. The truth is—

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.910
You guys must be thirsty.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.820
We'll go buy drinks.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.150
Thanks. I'd like melon soda.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:16.800
King Pudding for me.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.330
Okay. Melon soda and pudding, got it.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:22.210
We'll be back!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.540
What's up with them?

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.380
Hey!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.550
Let go of me.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.670
Iori, I'll buy you something, too.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:33.370
What?

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.180
You want ice cream? Taiyaki?

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.220
Are you trying to buy me off?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:39.890
With cheap sweets, no less.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.690
I'm broke!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.270
I'm going back and telling the others.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:47.980
I won't cause trouble for them!

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.990
I'll keep dancing even if it kills me.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:57.650
Nanase-san, your vocals 
are IDOLiSH7's weapon.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.910
Greatest weapon, even.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:05.220
As long as we have you, IDOLiSH7 
will someday stand in the sunlight.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.600
Is that a compliment?

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:10.650
Do I really have to say it?

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.930
No, I'm glad to hear it. Thanks.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.470
Like I was saying, your
 vocals are our weapon.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:21.510
Which is why your problem could also 
become the group's biggest bomb.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.520
If we're not careful, it could kill us.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.480
I know.

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.570
I know that.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:31.300
But I want to work with you guys.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.440
I want to keep doing 
IDOLiSH7 with all you guys.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:37.870
So please, I'm begging you. Don't tell them!

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.100
Nanase-san.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.220
Their manager sure was scary.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:53.260
Seriously.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:05.720
Anyway, what did Kujo mean when 
he said Riku can't stand onstage?

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.150
I wonder.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.240
It keeps coming down harder.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.600
We're supposed to announce our new song.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.870
Oh, my costume is wet.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.580
What should we do, Manager?

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.510
As long as the equipment can 
handle it, I think we can do it.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.280
Well...

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.190
Look at all those people.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.470
Maybe the trains have stopped running.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:38.970
Then let's do it.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:39.930
Huh?

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.570
You get bored when the trains don't run.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.430
Let's help them kill time.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.440
I agree. Let's entertain them 
until the train gets here.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.820
You're right.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:51.940
If we'll get wet anyway, 
let's dance before we leave.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:55.610
Yes! Dancing makes even rainy days fun.

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:56.650
Yeah.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:59.160
Got it. I'll have them get ready.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.410
Hey, Nanase-san.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:05.080
It's okay. I'll see this through.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.450
Get on standby, guys.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:10.710
Yeah!

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.300
This sucks.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.620
The train's not moving anytime soon.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.540
What time will I get home?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:21.140
Temporarily Suspended

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:30.900
Come on and dream the 
greatest of dreams Let's fly!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.060
<b>Mitsuki</b>

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:33.820
Thank you!

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:35.440
I7 is the best!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:38.740
Wow. Even in all this rain...

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.010
They look like they're having fun.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.950
Thank you! We are IDOLiSH7!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:49.340
Encore! Encore!

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:56.840
Encore! Encore!

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:52.230
Another encore.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:53.590
Even though the weather sucks!

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:54.890
Why not?

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:56.840
Let's keep going until 
the trains start running.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.840
Yeah. Let's do it again.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:04.320
Nanase-san, we'll sing the rest.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.260
You should rest.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.180
I'll keep singing until we're done.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.350
You can barely breathe.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.520
I can keep singing.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:17.300
I... I can stand onstage.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:22.200
Guys, thanks for the encore calls!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.570
We'll sing again!

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.090
Check it out!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.180
<i>As you can see,</i>

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:35.840
<i>the plaza in front of the station is packed 
with people waiting for the trains.</i>

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:38.290
We can start running

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:40.340
<i>And you can hear energetic 
voices singing in the crowd.</i>

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.340
(In this place that keeps changing)

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:45.810
Raise it up high, our Joker Flag

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:51.340
Kabuki Station

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:51.340
<b>Train service suspended due to heavy rain</b>

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:42.550
<i>Do you see this?</i>

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:47.010
<i>All these salarymen and 
students on their way home</i>

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:49.100
We'll clash (and search)

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:51.350
<i>are excited enough to blow this storm away.</i>

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.920
And someday turn into light

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.390
Run quickly

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.140
This voice...

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:55.530
Those guys who were on TV for a second.

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:59.150
And boldly Kira X Kira jump in (all right!)

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.270
They're IDOL...

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:58.760
IDOLiSH7.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.320
Yeah, them.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:04.740
Come on and dream the greatest of dreams

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:01.720
Rewind it.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:03.140
We're not recording.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.490
That idiot...

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.590
Train service has resumed!!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.510
Guys, the trains are running!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.240
You can go to back your warm homes now!

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.470
Thanks for tonight.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.570
I had tons of fun.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:31.060
I hope we can sing together again.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.890
We are IDOLiSH7!

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:33.420
Thank you.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.270
Later.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.230
Thank you.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:36.980
Thank you!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.730
I love I7!

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.730
I'll come see you next time!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.150
Good work.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.490
Thanks.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.850
That was really fun.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.870
Yeah. It was awesome.

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:55.730
Nanase-san.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:59.570
How long were we performing?

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.630
Two and a half hours.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.670
See? I did it.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.760
That's as long as a real concert.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.800
Even I can...

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.370
What does that mean?

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:13.610
Riku?

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:14.760
What's wrong, Riku?

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.270
Manager! Search Nanase-san's things!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.720
He should have an inhaler to handle attacks!

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:20.480
What?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.450
Got it!

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.440
An attack?

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.650
What kind of attack?

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:27.740
Nanase-san has a respiratory disorder.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:31.240
He can't engage in rigorous physical 
activity for extended periods of time.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:40.810
You're awake?

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:44.550
Tenn-nii, what are you doing here?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.540
I was worried about you.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.390
Now lie down.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:55.010
Tenn-nii, I'm trying to do what you do.

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:57.220
I want to sing and dance, too.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.320
Riku, you can't.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:00.940
Huh?

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.400
Watch and listen from down there.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.070
After all...

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:09.740
You'll never be able to leave that place.

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:11.100
Wait!

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.870
Bye-bye, Riku.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.790
I'm going with him.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.070
No! Wait!

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:18.430
Wait, Tenn-nii!

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:19.640
Don't go!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.790
Riku-san, you're awake?

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:30.440
Manager. Where am I?

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:33.350
The hospital. You should rest.

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.390
Um, Manager...

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:40.050
I'm sorry I didn't tell you about my illness.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:40.850
But, I—

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.850
Riku-san, why didn't you tell me?

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:45.780
Because...

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.510
I looked up your illness.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:51.510
You suffer attacks from rigorous 
physical activity, house dust,

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:54.410
and even changes in air pressure.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:55.790
Yes.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:58.540
If you'd told me, I could've helped you.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:14:59.790
Huh?

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:03.290
I'll clean the office so there's not 
a single one of Kinako's hairs left.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:05.880
What's wrong, Kinako?

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.630
We'll come up with lessons and concert 
plans that won't push you too hard.

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:13.170
You're not telling me to quit?

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:16.510
IDOLiSH7 needs you, Riku-san.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:19.530
It can't function without you.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:22.980
So from now on, no more hiding
 things. Tell me everything.

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:25.690
I will.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:32.740
When I first saw you, the 
desire to support someone—

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.800
to manage a group—took root inside me.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:42.080
So as long as you keep working, 
I'll keep on supporting you.

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.090
Manager...

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:48.470
I'm sorry I didn't notice 
how you were feeling.

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:50.790
No, it's my fault.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.170
Is there anything else you're hiding?

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:55.090
No.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:58.930
Are you okay?

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:00.960
I'm relieved.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.910
I thought you'd make me 
quit if you found out.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:08.980
Every time I tried to copy Tenn-nii, 
he told me I couldn't do it.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:09.810
Huh?

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:14.410
So that's what Kujo-san meant.

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:17.160
Huh? You met Tenn-nii?

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.620
Did he say anything about me?

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:22.680
Well, he rather harshly expressed 
some doubts about whether

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:25.420
or not you'd be able to perform onstage.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:29.460
I see. He's worried about me.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:32.340
Maybe he doesn't hate me.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.340
Maybe.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.930
He's just bothering people like us 
who are taking this seriously.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.110
Manager, I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:47.060
I look forward to continuing 
working with you.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.140
Me, too.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:54.030
Idol Street Performance Blows Away Storm??

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:54.030
Look. Everyone's talking about the concert.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.040
They broadcast it?

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:57.850
Could you see my face?

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.410
Considering the weather, I'm not so sure.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:05.230
I'm so glad we got fans from that concert.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.170
I'm just glad they enjoyed it.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.030
We had fun, too.

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:12.170
Yes. It was exciting.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:15.770
It felt like we were causing the storm.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:19.170
Other music news sites are 
covering the story, too.

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:21.460
We've even received requests to appear

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:24.310
at company events for some of 
the people who were watching.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:28.190
Looks like that concert gave everyone 
the impression you're an energetic group.

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.610
Seriously? I'm so happy.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:34.980
Oh, right. Riku-san and 
Iori-san have a fan site, too.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.780
Really? Lemme see!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.620
<b><Unofficial>

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.620
Apparently, they like you two together.

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:43.080
<b><Unofficial>

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.080
Why?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.860
Having such passionate fans makes me happy.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:47.960
Yamato-san gets a lot of fan letters.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.440
Someone made a fan for you, Mitsu.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.420
I was moved when I saw it the other day.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:59.690
Oh. Sogo receives luxurious gifts 
from anonymous senders once a week.

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:01.220
I'm really grateful for them.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:05.110
Our stock of CDs ran out, 
so we've ordered more.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:08.350
And every day we get more SNS followers.

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:11.860
All these people support us.

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:14.260
Let me see more.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.450
Me, too.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:17.030
Hey, I can't see!

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.320
Let's keep broadening our scope.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:24.720
With sincerity, so their voices 
will reach even farther.

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:25.530
Yes.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:27.040
Manager.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.040
Yes?

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:30.040
Do you have a minute?

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.540
Iori-san, do you need something?

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.050
The wind is blowing our way.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:37.290
Now's the time to act.

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:38.930
Another outdoor concert?

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:40.440
At that venue?

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:42.950
What if only nine people show up again?

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:45.180
Th-This time we'll fill the stands.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.280
You don't sound so sure.

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.240
Fill them!

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:48.950
Oh.

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.770
Don't worry.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:53.220
We can create currents ourselves.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:57.390
Our previous concert was a disaster, 
but there was one benefit.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:58.490
What benefit?

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:00.280
What was it?

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:04.240
Oh. The experience of performing 
at a large venue?

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.700
Correct.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.620
And since we're not famous yet,

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:12.790
we retain only the experience 
of performing at a large venue,

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.840
and rumors of our disastrous 
concert didn't spread.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:20.630
So, even if we perform at the same venue again, 
we'll be able to get three thousand people.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.970
You think so?

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:25.170
I'm worried.

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:28.060
And I wouldn't want to take away 
the president's side dishes again.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.250
You old men are pathetic.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.100
What?

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.840
I wanna do it.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:35.360
Yes! I agree.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:38.230
Yeah. We'll never get 
anywhere if we don't try.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:41.080
Well, I'd actually like to try it.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.900
Yeah, I think it's a good idea.

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:45.370
The young don't hesitate, do they?

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:49.000
Fine. Let's try it.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.390
Guys...

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:53.170
Thank you.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:56.290
Let me handle promoting
 the event and everything else.

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:59.800
Let's work hard to prepare for the concert!

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.810
Congratulations on your outdoor concert!

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:06.300
I'll definitely go!

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:08.720
Thank you. We'll be waiting.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.480
That was so fun.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:15.730
Hey, let me go with you 
to their next concert.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.730
Seriously? Let's go to the 
outdoor concert, then.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.830
Yeah.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:23.990
Oh, but we might need to take 
the day tickets go on sale off.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:25.240
Why?

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.780
Because...

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:30.290
They're only letting 
three thousand people in.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.040
Ticket Details > Reserve Tickets > Confirm Reservation > Complete

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.040
IDOLiSH7 We are eternal Dreamers!!

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.160
Sales start in a minute.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:39.430
I'm really nervous.

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.620
Are you okay? The stress isn't good for you.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:44.430
So, your face is super tense, too.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:47.200
My stomach hurts.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.630
Unbelievable.

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:50.470
Calm down, everyone.

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:56.680
Please let them sell out, please let 
them sell out, please let them sell out.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:55.730
Manager, calm down.

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:57.430
It's time!

00:20:57.540 --> 00:21:01.230
Reserve Tickets

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:01.230
This site is experiencing connection 
issues due to a high volume of traffic. 

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:01.230
Huh?

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.960
Huh? What?

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:04.450
We can't tell what's going on.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.120
Boys.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.450
The ticket site contacted us.

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:12.450
They've sold out!

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:13.640
What?

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:15.940
Sold out?

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:19.710
Ye—

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.710
Wait.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.640
It's too early to celebrate.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:24.220
Are you sure you didn't mishear them?

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.410
No, I don't think so.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:32.220
Yes! Congratulations!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.230
All right!

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.560
Wow. Last time it was only nine.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.270
They're all coming.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:42.620
Manager? Are you asleep?

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:44.960
I'm so happy...

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:46.410
Here, Manager.

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:50.120
Thank you, Sogo-san.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:54.620
I told you we'd definitely 
sell all three thousand.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:56.410
That's not all.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:00.080
We were also contacted by a music 
program on a local TV station.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.170
They want to broadcast the concert.

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:03.300
TV?

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:05.320
What?

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:06.880
B-Broadcast?

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:09.720
I wasn't expecting that.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.640
Congratulations, boys.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:12.930
Sir.

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:17.350
Let's celebrate with Korean barbecue tonight.

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:23.940
Yeah!

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.950
Start running (beyond)

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:44.960
Your imagination... Alive

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:58.610
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:03.270
Risk your life and dive in

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:08.360
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:13.490
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:16.390
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:18.580
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:21.460
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:26.380
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:32.450
You'll be the first witness

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.240
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:42.190
Admit that you can't deny it

00:23:42.530 --> 00:23:46.650
We start... What do your fingertips

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:51.260
Seek now?
